[INFO] 09-21 20:15:56 run_experiments.py:122] **Strategy Formulation**: 1. Determine the prime factorization of 20! and list its distinct prime factors (primes ≤ 20: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19). 2. Count the number of distinct primes, denoted as \( k \) (which is 8). 3. Calculate the number of coprime pairs \( (a,b) \) with \( a \times b = 20! \) as \( 2^k \). Since half of these pairs have \( a < b \) (corresponding to fractions between 0 and 1) and none have \( a = b \) (as 20! is not a perfect square), compute the final count using the formula \( N = 2^{k-1} \).
